From e21eca1b099cd297d39c95491319a726bb35ee36 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gf691271 <gf691271@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 01:43:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat: a 15 min keepalive that only reconnects
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Root cause of the lost night of 2026-11-15: the app was restarted at 22:02 and never
reconnected. `general_autoconnectonbluetooth` defaults to false, so a plain restart does not
connect, and nothing else initiates one — Gadgetbridge's own retry only runs while the state is
WAITING_FOR_RECONNECT, which is not the state after a restart. The device therefore sat in
NOT_CONNECTED until a manual tap at 00:14 and the whole sleep window produced no beats.

PERIODIC_SYNC would have connected at 02:00, i.e. two hours into the window, and with a 6 h
interval on an 8 h window it can miss the night entirely.

- KeepAliveReceiver: on fire, logs every device that is neither connected nor initialized and
  calls deviceService.connect() once if there is any. No sync, no fetch.
- KeepAliveScheduler: 15 min chained `setAndAllowWhileIdle`, armed from GBApplication.onCreate,
  gated by `pref_keepalive_connect` (default true), mirroring PeriodicSyncScheduler but without
  the TYPE_SYNC that makes that one too heavy to run every 15 min.
- Manifest: receiver registered, exported=false.

Together with the 0005 liveness watchdog this covers the three ways the link goes quiet:
restart without reconnect (this), NOT_CONNECTED with no trigger (this), and a half-open socket
that still reports CONNECTED (0005).

Compiled: assembleMainlineDebug BUILD_OK. Not installed yet: the night capture is running.
